<title>PHILIPPINES: Reynolds set to okay cap hike, dividend.</title>
<headline>Reynolds set to okay cap hike, dividend.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stockholders of Reynolds Philippines Corp are set to approve an increase of its authorised capital to one billion pesos and a 42.8 percent stock dividend, chief financial officer Jorge Navarra said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Navarra told reporters after the listing of Reynolds' 238 million common shares on the Philippine Stock Exchange that the capital increase would ratified at a special stockholders' meeting which is scheduled at noon.</p>
<p>The aluminium producer currently has a capital of 700 million pesos.</p>
<p>Shareholders as of February 14 would be eligible for the dividend, if approved, Navarra added.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
